    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0790" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.22793/6–2746</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Patterson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-07-18">July 18, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The receipt is
                    acknowledged of your letter of June 27, 1946,<anchor n="17" xml:id="d468-f1"/>
                    regarding the necessity of providing the War Department with funds to continue
                    the Chinese Air Force Training Program after June 30, 1946.</p>
                <pb facs="0791" n="781" xml:id="pg781"/>
                <p>Reference is made in this connection to my letter of July 10, 1946,<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d468-f2"/> in which it was stated that on June 29, 1946, a check for
                    $4,000,000 was delivered by representatives of the Chinese Government to the War
                    Department as an initial payment in support of the Air Force Training Program
                    after June 30, 1946. The Department of State will continue to make every effort
                    to obtain from the Chinese Government the balance due so that there will be no
                    interruption in the program.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dean Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
